-- A program that names its own value JOIN or DEADLINE (the nouns are not
-- reserved words) and writes THE in front of it. Before 2026-10-24 THE
-- was an optional article there, and `WITH start IS THE JOIN` passed the
-- program's own 100. Since the nouns are values (EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC
-- §2.6 card B1), THE JOIN is always the lifecycle position.
--
-- Under a HENCE that changes the answer with no error: the refund below
-- falls due at 4 + 30 = 34 instead of 100 + 30 = 130. So the checker warns
-- wherever THE is written before a noun the program also defines
-- (LifecycleNounHidesName), and the warning says how to reach the value:
-- drop the THE. JOIN is defined in this module, so renaming it is offered
-- too; for an imported JOIN it is not. jl4-service refuses to deploy a
-- module that draws this warning (B1a). At the top level the same
-- spelling is also refused outright, because THE DEADLINE has no
-- obligation to read there; the warning comes with the refusal, so the
-- drafter learns why the spelling changed meaning. The `DEADLINE` without THE is the program's value and
-- draws nothing.

IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Refund  HAS who IS AN Actor

alice MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"

JOIN MEANS 100
DEADLINE MEANS 5

GIVEN start IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`refund within 30 of` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Refund alice WITHIN 30 OF start

-- warned, and the run uses the join (4), not the program's JOIN (100)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`passes THE JOIN` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE `refund within 30 of` WITH start IS THE JOIN

-- not warned: JOIN without THE is the program's value
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`passes JOIN` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE `refund within 30 of` WITH start IS JOIN

GIVEN start IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
f MEANS start PLUS 1

-- refused (no obligation at the top level) and warned
#EVAL f WITH start IS THE DEADLINE
-- the program's value: 6
#EVAL f WITH start IS DEADLINE
